<title>GERMANY: Siemens workers protest job cuts.</title>
<headline>Siemens workers protest job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 2,000 workers in Siemens AG's medical equipment division demonstrated on Thursday against plans to cut 1,000 jobs, union officials said.</p>
<p>The workers paraded in automobiles through the town of Erlangen, and then held a rally in front of the Siemens administration building.</p>
<p>A union spokesman said job actions would continue, with five meetings scheduled in the coming week to inform the division's 6,500 employees about management's plans.</p>
<p>The union has suggested the workweek be reduced to 30 hours with a corresponding pay cut to save the jobs.</p>
<p>A division spokesman said the company needs to take rationalisation measures to build up its competitive strength.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
